# Line endings.
#
# This repo is authored on Windows but built on Linux and macOS CI runners, which
# is exactly the situation that silently breaks shell scripts. `android/gradlew`
# is a POSIX shell script: if Git ever checks it out with CRLF, the runner fails
# with a `bad interpreter: /bin/sh^M` error that looks nothing like a line-ending
# problem. Normalising to LF in the repository prevents that class of bug for
# every text file, and the two exceptions below cover the cases that genuinely
# need CRLF or must not be touched at all.

* text=auto eol=lf

# Windows-only launcher — cmd.exe wants CRLF.
*.bat text eol=crlf

# Gradle wrapper: LF, always, no exceptions. Stated explicitly rather than left
# to `text=auto` so it survives someone relaxing the rule above.
gradlew text eol=lf
gradlew.bat text eol=crlf

# Binary: never munge, never diff as text.
*.png binary
*.jpg binary
*.webp binary
*.ico binary
*.woff2 binary
*.jar binary
*.apk binary
*.aab binary
*.keystore binary
*.jks binary
